 ## Profile settings
 
+### GFG fork: Autopilot-owned Fusion scope
+
+`gfg_frame_fusion` is a boolean live profile extension, default false in the Renderer. GFG stable 2.1.0 sets it only in an enabled Autopilot runtime overlay. The launch environment permits resource provisioning; execution requires both applied and requested scopes. Leaving scope closes raw source transfers and direct scaler inputs immediately, retaining an ordinary same-format blit until the existing private-group transition commits. Native candidates require blit features for this safe retained-group path. The optional Fusion extension publishes Autopilot scope capability.
+
 ### Frame Generation
 
 | Setting | Default | Meaning |
diff --git a/engine/docs/MEMORY-MANAGEMENT.md b/engine/docs/MEMORY-MANAGEMENT.md
index c065d6e..a1c293b 100644
--- a/engine/docs/MEMORY-MANAGEMENT.md
+++ b/engine/docs/MEMORY-MANAGEMENT.md
@@ -129,3 +129,13 @@ ## Validation and change ownership
 | Scaling admission and resource formats | [`spatial_scaling_policy.hpp`](../mako-render/src/spatial_scaling_policy.hpp), [`spatial_scaler.cpp`](../mako-render/src/spatial_scaler.cpp) |
 
 Extend these owners when changing memory behavior. Keep the allocator, accounting, failure cleanup, focused tests, and owning boundary guide aligned; do not add a second allocator or treat a policy estimate as completion or allocation proof.
+
+## Experimental direct sampled FG inputs
+
+The GFG Frame Fusion patch owns bounded descriptor bindings in `SpatialScaler`, borrowing generated-image views from the swapchain. Bindings must be drained and cleared before replacing or destroying their images, including prepared scalers, backend transitions and retirement. Setup is transactional and recording performs no allocations. Descriptors only accept matching extent/format, sampled usage, unique handles and at most 64 inputs. This patch retains the private fallback images; it removes one copy on an eligible recorded path, not the full memory allocation.
+
+## Experimental native-resolution source transport
+
+GFG Native Fusion keeps two private history images and their existing FD/timeline ownership. For equal-resolution SDR8 UNORM input without a spatial scaler, `fusion_source_transport.hpp` selects a matching RGBA8 or BGRA8 source layout. Both application and backend devices must support the matching sampled transfer image and opaque-FD export/import. Exporter and importer use `TRANSFER_DST | SAMPLED`; model descriptors only sample these images. The backend's SDR8 model, intermediate/output formats, scheduler and retirement remain unchanged. The old `openContext` signature selects the default transport; an explicit source-layout overload owns the same FD batch before construction.
+
+The canonical private-resource builder constructs the complete source/destination/semaphore/context group before commit. One failed native construction releases its temporary resources and tries the default source layout once. Successful replacement resets native counters; failed startup clears native preparation and retains application presentation. A native source submission uses same-format `vkCmdCopyImage` rather than a conversion blit; it does not remove either history image or the source transfer. Publication schema 2 reports native transfers and BGRA conversion blits separately from spatial copy elimination. Counters describe submitted work, not GPU completion, session totals, power or performance gains.
