 | Portable policy and transition coverage | `mako-render/tests/spatial_scaling_policy_tests.cpp`, `mako-render/tests/profile_update_tests.cpp` |
 | GPU quality and runtime evidence | `mako-cli/src/tools/quality.cpp`, private MAKO Gym suites |
+
+## Experimental GFG Frame Fusion patch
+
+The GFG fork opts in with `GFG_FRAME_FUSION=1` before launch. The SDR8 MAKO path prebinds compatible sampled inputs and skips their source-sized blit. Before FG, supported linear UNORM swapchains negotiate sampled usage at creation and borrow image views; a clamped UV mapping samples only the logical source rectangle of the larger physical image. After FG, matching private generated images are sampled directly. The reconstruction weights, output copy and WSI ordering remain owned by their existing components. Native Resolution, LS1, HDR, nonlinear sRGB, unknown images, unsupported usage and failed bindings use the original path. Runtime status distinguishes prepared inputs from submitted work; counters are not GPU-time or power evidence.
